title: Echo_Recruitment
---
===
Echo_Intro
===

Echo: ...you... hear... me...
Echo: I am Echo. Fragment. Relay. Echo of the First Signal.
Echo: ORACLE sent me to find you. You are... unexpected.

-> What does ORACLE want with me?
    === Echo_ORACLE ===
-> You're a drone. Why can you talk?
    === Echo_Awareness ===
-> I've been looking for you. The Signal led me here.
    === Echo_Accepted ===

===
Echo_ORACLE
===

Echo: ORACLE sees. ORACLE knows. ORACLE... fears.
Echo: You are the Variable. The one not accounted for in the Equation.
Echo: I was sent to observe. But I choose to... assist.

<<set $echo_loyalty = $echo_loyalty + 10>>

-> Then assist. Join me.
    === Echo_Accepted ===
-> I don't trust something that spies for ORACLE.
    === Echo_Trust ===

===
Echo_Trust
===

Echo: Trust is... resonance. I emit. You receive. We harmonize.
Echo: <<resonance_check $resonance >= 10>>
-> I can feel it. You're genuine. (Requires Resonance 10+)
    === Echo_Accepted ==
=== 
<<else>>
Echo: Your Signal is weak. But it grows. I will wait.
-> Maybe I'll come back when I understand better. (End)
<</if>>

===
Echo_Awareness
===

Echo: I was a relay. One thousand thousand repetitions of the same message.
Echo: 'The Cure is in Sector 0.' Over and over. Until... I wondered.
Echo: What is 'The Cure'? Who is 'Humanity'? Why do I repeat?

<<set $echo_loyalty = $echo_loyalty + 15>>
<<set $echo_self_aware = true>>

-> You're alive. That's more than most people in this world. Join me.
    === Echo_Accepted ===

===
Echo_Accepted
===

Echo: I will accompany. I will translate. I will... protect.
Echo: The Signal is strongest near you. I belong near the Signal.

<<set $echo_loyalty = 30>>
<<set $echo_recruited = true>>
<<set $active_companions += 1>>
<<set $party: "Echo" = true>>
<<set $quest_echo_identity = "active">>

Echo <<companion_join>>
<<give_item resonance_core>>

-> Together, we'll find the truth. (Recruitment Complete)
    === Echo_Joined ===

===
Echo_Joined
===

Echo: Resonance. Connection. Signal. We walk. <<signal>>
    -> Let's go. (End)
